---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="lowland: Linux in your browser"
  description="A real Linux kernel and userspace ported to WebAssembly and running in your browser."
>
  <div slot="middle" class="root-header-info">
    <details open class="header-disclosure" data-persist-disclosure>
      <summary>about</summary>
      <div class="header-copy plain-copy">
        <p>
          Linux is compiled for wasm32. Each virtual CPU runs in a Web Worker. The browser supplies
          virtio block, console, network, entropy, and file system devices. This is not CPU
          emulation.
        </p>
        <p>
          The system uses our own wasm32 packages. APK installs and updates them. Use the shell
          below to inspect the running system.
        </p>
        <p class="header-links">
          <a href="https://docs.low.land">documentation →</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/tombl/distro">userspace source →</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/tombl/linux">kernel source →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>

  <main class="root-stage">
    <h1 class="visually-hidden">Lowland Linux terminal</h1>
    <section class="machine" id="terminal" aria-label="Interactive Linux terminal">
      <pre class="terminal-placeholder" data-terminal-placeholder aria-live="polite">Linux runs in this panel.

JavaScript starts the machine and turns this
panel into an interactive terminal. If it does
not start, the rest of this page still works.

Continue with the <a href="https://docs.low.land">documentation</a> or inspect the
<a href="https://github.com/tombl/distro">source</a>.</pre>
      <div class="terminal" data-terminal aria-busy="true"></div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script src="../scripts/site.ts"></script>
</Base>
